@startuml
!theme plain
actor Driver
participant "Driver View" as UI
participant "Entry API\nDriverRouteController" as API
participant "RouteSendService" as SVC
database "MySQL" as DB

title S-2/S-3 Driver views assigned routes

Driver -> UI: Login (role DRIVER, shared auth)
UI -> API: GET /api/v1/driver/routes
API -> SVC: listMine(driverId)
SVC -> DB: CURRENT sends first, then SUPERSEDED
SVC --> API: Assigned routes (own only; 403 on foreign ids)
API --> UI: List (banner: new version available if SUPERSEDED exist)
Driver -> UI: Open route detail
UI -> API: GET /api/v1/driver/routes/{sendId}
API -> SVC: detail(sendId, driverId)
alt foreign sendId (F-S2 403)
  SVC --> API: 403
  API --> UI: "No access" + back to list
else data missing (F-S2)
  SVC --> API: 404
  API --> UI: Error toast + back to list (record untouched)
else ok
  SVC -> DB: Route + stops + orderId->Order join (phone, notes)
  SVC --> API: Stops in sequence + ETA + contacts + version flag
  API --> UI: Render detail
end

note over UI: Session expiry at any step -> 401 ->\nlogin -> return to the same view (F-S2).
@enduml
